{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"OESA-2026-3411","published":"2026-08-20T09:54:49Z","modified":"2026-08-20T10:15:06.398270925Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-15779"],"summary":"samba security update","details":"Samba is a suite of programs for Linux and Unix to interoperate with Windows.\r\n\r\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\nA flaw was found in samba&apos;s pam_winbind. When mkhomedir is enabled, pam_winbind chowns the target account&apos;s home directory without validating the path is not a critical system directory such as /. On affected systems, accounts with / as their home directory (a common default for system accounts) can have this triggered not only by root, but by a non-root user holding a narrow sudo delegation to run commands as that account, causing ownership of / to change and resulting in severe denial of service (SSH, sudo, and package-manager failures). The change does not grant write access to / (which ships with restrictive 0555 permissions on RHEL), so the impact is availability loss rather than further privilege escalation.(CVE-2026-15779)","affected":[{"package":{"name":"samba","ecosystem":"openEuler:24.03-LTS-SP3","purl":"pkg:rpm/openEuler/samba&distro=openEuler-24.03-LTS-SP3"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"4.19.3-11.oe2403sp3"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"aarch64":["ctdb-4.19.3-11.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","libsmbclient-4.19.3-11.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","libsmbclient-devel-4.19.3-11.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","libwbclient-4.19.3-11.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","libwbclient-devel-4.19.3-11.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","python3-samba-4.19.3-11.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","python3-samba-dc-4.19.3-11.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","python3-samba-test-4.19.3-11.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","samba-4.19.3-11.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","samba-client-4.19.3-11.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","samba-client-libs-4.19.3-11.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","samba-common-4.19.3-11.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","samba-common-tools-4.19.3-11.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","samba-dc-4.19.3-11.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","